class.description:
A [TimerInstance] is a timer of [TimerServer] that is created in code with [method TimerServer.create_timer]. It has the same methods and signals as the [Timer] node, but needs no node in the scene tree. It is stopped until [method start] is called.
A running instance is kept alive by [TimerServer], so you do not have to store a reference to it. Its timer is freed when the instance is freed: in GDScript as soon as it has ended and no reference is left; in C#, the wrapper object holds a reference until the garbage collector collects it.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var info = TimerInfo.new()
info.total_time = 2.5
var timer = TimerServer.create_timer(info)
timer.start()
await timer.timeout
print("Done")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var info = new TimerInfo();
info.TotalTime = 2.5;
TimerInstance timer = TimerServer.CreateTimer(info);
timer.Start();
await ToSignal(timer, TimerInstance.SignalName.Timeout);
GD.Print("Done");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
